          "Consolidate the college-educated, white middle-class base that currently holds the 59% while building bridges to working-class households regardless of educational attainment: the $67,990 median income and 37.4% college rate describe a district split between relative stability and economic pressure. Messaging that addresses healthcare cost, childcare affordability, wage trajectory, and small-business viability speaks to both constituencies and prevents the division from becoming a partisan opening.",
