          "Engage the 6.78% demographic gap explicitly—likely American Indian/Alaska Native residents whose constituent needs and political preferences are not visible in partisan aggregates. Active constituent service and genuine engagement with this population is both a governance obligation and a hedge against a future challenger who mobilizes this currently-invisible constituency.",
          "Consolidate the college-educated suburban vote (27.5% college attainment in a mixed-education district): this group evaluates on education funding quality, research and innovation support, and workforce development. A legislative agenda that treats education as an economic investment, not an ideological battleground, better reflects the district's actual educational composition.",
          "Do not campaign this seat as if 64% represents structural safety: in a district with 35% renters, 39.2-year median age, and moderate income, a credible challenger focused on cost-of-living performance could rapidly narrow the margin if incumbent constituent service is perceived as weak or if the unaccounted demographic gap is mobilized."
