          "Lead on renter economic security and housing policy: at 25.3%, renters represent one-quarter of the district and are the demographic most likely to be persuadable on the basis of specific economic policy — housing affordability, tenant protections, or service delivery — rather than partisan loyalty.",
          "Engage education and workforce development with specificity: the 21.3% college-educated population and younger workforce are evaluating on whether the district's schools and community colleges are preparing them for regional economic opportunity; generic conservative rhetoric on education does not address this constituency's material concerns.",
          "Build authentic relationships with AIAN constituents and tribal governments: the ~10.3% demographic gap requires proactive engagement rather than passive assumption; this community's turnout and candidate preference are not predetermined by the current partisan result and represent a genuine swing dynamic in a 63-37 seat."
