          { name: "Assuming the 62% Margin Reflects a Stable, Consolidated Coalition", tag: "avoid", why: "A 62-38 result is a solid margin but not a landslide, and it is held by a coalition that spans educated white homeowners and Hispanic voters with potentially different economic priorities. In a district with a low renter rate but still meaningful Hispanic presence, demographic change and shifting evaluations of whether government is serving both communities effectively could erode this margin in future cycles. A representative who campaigns this seat as safe and relies on base consolidation rather than active constituency engagement is setting the stage for unexpected vulnerability." }
