          "Lead with fiscal responsibility and education investment as an integrated agenda: in a district with 32.4% college attainment and high median income, this constituency believes public education is foundational to community quality and economic vitality; demonstrate how conservative fiscal stewardship and strong K-12 funding coexist rather than compete.",
          "Engage the 25.1% renter population and Hispanic/Asian/multiracial constituents (nearly 18% of the district) with specific policy attention to housing affordability, tenant protections, and pathways to homeownership; in a 51-49 race, losing these constituencies to demographic assumptions or passive outreach is a credible path to defeat.",
          "Treat a 51% result as a plurality, not a majority: the combination of affluent, educated swing voters with real policy concerns and a nearly 18% non-white population creates a district where persuasion and turnout discipline are essential every cycle—not a seat where consolidating the existing coalition while ignoring the opposition is a viable strategy."
