          { name: "Ignoring the 9.29% Hispanic Constituency or Treating It as Peripheral", tag: "avoid", why: "In a district this demographically homogeneous and affluent, a 9.29% Hispanic population that is not specifically engaged risks becoming invisible in both representation and political participation. Hispanic constituents in an $86,000-median-income district have economic interests, school involvement, and civic participation patterns that deserve direct attention rather than assumption into a broader white homeowner narrative. A representative who ignores this community signals that Hispanic residents are not fully part of the constituency being served—a political vulnerability if Democrats build a specific engagement strategy around economic mobility and recognition." }
