          "Engage affluent suburban women specifically on healthcare, education, and reproductive rights: college-educated female voters in high-income suburbs are the swing constituency most likely to evaluate a candidate as an individual rather than a party representative, and their policy concerns are concrete, not symbolic.",
          "Address housing affordability and renter protection despite low renter rate: the 24.8% renter rate includes younger professionals and service-sector workers for whom housing costs may be the primary economic constraint; ignoring renter concerns in a district with 45% opposition is losing an active persuadable constituency."
