          { name: "Defaulting to Homeowner-Majority Preferences on Development & Housing", tag: "avoid", why: "In a district with a 40.9% renter rate, development and housing policy decisions that exclusively benefit homeowners — restrictive zoning, opposition to apartment development, rent-control resistance — will generate political opposition among renters and younger adults even within the Democratic supermajority. An incumbent who consistently prioritizes homeowner preferences on housing and development is vulnerable to being challenged from within the coalition by renter-focused candidates, particularly if renters perceive that housing costs are rising faster than wages. This is an internal coalition risk, not an external electoral one." }
