          "Engage the 36.2% renter population with specific policy: rent stabilization, tenant protections, and wage growth tied to cost-of-living are not fringe demands in a district where more than one-third of households rent—they are constituent needs that the incumbent must address substantively or lose to a challenger who does.",
          "Recognize the 11.61% Hispanic community as a swing constituency capable of meaningful turnout and preference shifts; in a six-point-margin district, community-specific engagement on economic opportunity, education access, and family stability is not optional—it is the difference between holding and losing."
