          { name: "Overlooking Demographic Change and the Diversity of the Professional Coalition", tag: "avoid", why: "WA-HD-46's 70.8% college-educated, 15.73% Asian, 34.8-year median age composition is not static—the district's professional workforce, ethnic composition, and generational character continue to evolve. An incumbent or challenger who campaigns as though the district is defined primarily by white college-educated voters and treats Asian, Hispanic, and other minority constituencies as secondary risks missing the evolving coalition and alienating communities that are becoming more central to the district's identity. Visible, ongoing engagement with demographic change is a governance requirement, not a political nice-to-have." }
