          { name: "Treating Small-Business Community as Monolithic", tag: "avoid", why: "The $77,791 median household income and 50.9% renter rate indicate a working-class district, not an entrepreneurial one, but that does not mean small-business owners are absent or irrelevant to the constituency. Broadly anti-business messaging or class-conflict framing that positions small employers as enemies rather than as part of the working community risks alienating the ~15-20% of the district whose household income and economic security depend on local business viability. The incumbent's 63% margin likely includes small-business owners who have concluded that Democratic priorities around worker protections and neighborhood stability serve their interests better than Republican alternatives — but that judgment is contingent on not feeling stereotyped as exploiters or treated as policy obstacles rather than as constituent stakeholders." }
