          "Build a specific housing and renter-community strategy: the 25.6% renter population in an affluent suburban district tends to be younger and more Democratic, but often persuadable on economic mobility and housing affordability; ignoring this quarter of the electorate cedes a swing constituency to the opposition.",
          "Avoid weaponizing cultural issues or treating education and affluence as liability: college-educated voters making $90k+ are responsive to competence signals, economic security, and governance delivery — not to cultural grievance positioning that reads as dismissive of their lived priorities around healthcare, climate, and institutional trust."
