          "Address renter and working-class economic security: With 33.1% renters and $73,188 median income, this is a district where housing costs consume a larger share of household budgets than statewide averages. Specific policy positions on rent stabilization, tenant protections, and wage policy directly address the material concerns of a third of the district—and are precisely the issues that can shift working-class voters in competitive suburban/exurban races.",
          "Recognize that unopposed does not equal safe: The 2024 unopposed result reflects Democratic challenger absence, not Republican strength. In a district with 30% Hispanic population, 33% renters, and sub-$75k median income, a credible Democratic challenger with resources and a coherent economic message could plausibly compete. Any incumbent complacency about this margin is strategically dangerous.",
