          "Address fiscal fairness and tax policy with specificity: a 49% Republican result in an affluent suburb signals meaningful conservative skepticism about government spending or tax burden; the incumbent must articulate a clear tax philosophy that resonates with voters who are financially secure enough to evaluate opportunity costs.",
          "Engage the 27.5% renter constituency as a distinct constituency with distinct concerns: younger renters have different economic priorities around housing affordability, student debt, and entry-level opportunity than homeowners; visibility on these issues prevents the district from becoming a purely homeowner conversation."
