          "Engage the 7.57% demographic gap explicitly: the unaccounted-for population of Hispanic, Asian, Native American, Black, and mixed-race residents represents a constituency whose economic concerns, educational priorities, and civic participation are not being adequately addressed by either party — building an explicit coalition that names these communities and delivers on their specific governance concerns (equitable school funding, healthcare access, economic mobility) is the path to a durable 55%+ result.",
          "Address cost-of-living pressures head-on: in a district this affluent, the fact that one-quarter of residents are renting and the median income is $102k indicates meaningful financial anxiety among educated professionals — property tax fairness, housing affordability, childcare costs, and healthcare coverage are the material concerns driving swing voters, not partisan messaging."
