          "Lead with quality-of-life delivery for high-income homeowners: housing costs and zoning, property tax management, school quality and funding, infrastructure maintenance, and cost-of-living pressures are the material concerns of $102k median household professionals and families. Generic partisan messaging on these issues will not move voters who are evaluating on whether their representative is solving their specific problems.",
          "Engage the Latino and Asian communities with specificity rather than absorption into a generic 'coalition' narrative: at 7.69% and 3.88% respectively, these communities are meaningful in a 51-49 district, and their concerns around economic mobility, education pathways, and equitable service delivery deserve direct attention, not symbolic recognition.",
          "Build accountability to a 51% margin: the district's resources, education level, and income mean that voters can and will evaluate performance in detail. Regular constituent feedback, measurable delivery on stated priorities, and transparent communication about what is and is not achievable are the governance behaviors that either consolidate or erode a margin this narrow."
