          "Address college-educated white voter retention explicitly: this constituency, at ~39% of the district and concentrated in urban professional demographics, is the most electorally mobile within the Democratic coalition and most likely to evaluate on specific governance performance rather than partisan loyalty; concrete delivery on housing affordability, transportation, and public safety is necessary to hold this vote.",
          "Build housing-cost solutions into core legislative identity: at 51% renters with a $96,922 median income, substantial portions of the district face housing-cost burden; tenant protection, zoning reform, and development policy that connects income levels to housing availability are direct constituent concerns that will determine whether younger and more mobile voters remain engaged.",
          "Do not treat unopposed incumbency as permission to reduce constituency presence; Democratic districts with high diversity and high education are precisely the districts where strong challengers emerge when incumbents become disconnected from constituent service; maintain proportional investment in district presence, responsive constituent services, and community presence across all major demographic communities."
